From: MiaAI_Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Subject: glm-cuda: the GB10 window and shared cost tables as this pair measures them

The two compile-time tables price a verify forward for the lane core (lanes/config.zig: window_costs is "forward ms
by exact window width", shared_costs is "shared forwards' ms by total rows"). Both were over-priced on this pair.

Measured on spark3 + spark4 (GB10 x2, TP=2, EXL3 4 bpw, q8 dense, bf16 head, fp8 KV on pages, DFlash2 at 4 bits) on
2026-11-03, from 587 TF_GLM_DFLASH2_TRACE records taken with TF_GLM_DFLASH2_FORCE=1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8 cycled so every
width is sampled inside one run. A record's v= is the wall ms of exactly one verify forward (cuda_lanes.zig's
observe call sites), which is the same quantity the tables hold, so the comparison is like-for-like. Shared records
were regrouped into forwards (consecutive w=0 records carrying the identical ms) and fitted against the forward's
total rows, which is what shared_costs.get(rows) is indexed by (lanes/depth.zig).

  lone windows, 309 observations, medians 37.97 44.77 50.89 56.03 61.27 66.23 73.05 78.55 ms at 1..8 rows
    fit 38.73 + 5.68 (rows - 1), r2 0.9983, residuals within +-0.9 ms     table said 52.0 + 6.8
  shared forwards, 139 observations of two lanes each, 2..16 total rows
    fit 47.38 + 5.05 (rows - 1), r2 0.9934                                table said 76.0 + 4.1

costTable's `one` is the ms at width 1 (i = 0 gives width 1), the same convention as the fit, so there is no
one-row offset between them.

Why this is worth a patch rather than a note. lanes/depth.zig's observeOverhead learns the scheduler's overhead as
`ms - shared_costs.get(rows)`, clamped at zero, and feeds it to allocateDrafts, which is the adaptive input to
cross-stream draft allocation. At the old constants a shared forward of 4 total rows was priced at 76.0 + 4.1*3 =
88.3 ms against a measured 62.0, so the subtraction went negative and the learner was starved: taking a forward's
measured ms plus its drafter pass as a lower bound on the round, only 4 of the 139 measured two-lane forwards could
have produced a positive term, against 133 of 139 at the prices here, where it learns 3 to 8 ms. Starved, not dead
-- the round ms the learner is actually given is larger than that lower bound, so the old rate may be above 4/139.
Whether learning it improves throughput is a question for the A/B, not a claim of this patch.

Exact: scheduling only. No kernel, no reduction order and no token changes, so the ship check is identical greedy
token ids (tensorfold.token_sha on a fixed corpus) plus the throughput gate, not an NLL comparison.

Not measured here: forwards of more than two lanes. The shared fit is two-lane data, and a four-lane forward's
fixed cost may differ; the table is still far closer to the truth than 76.0 at every width measured.

diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig
--- a/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/glm/cuda_lanes.zig
@@ -20,9 +20,13 @@
 const mtp_rows = 1 + engine.max_drafts;
 const max_held = dflash.BLOCK - 1; // a DFlash2 block's drafts (the MTP head's chains stop at max_drafts)
 
-/// With DFlash2: a window's ms by rows on two GB10s (EXL3, TF_GLM_PROF: 86 to 107 ms at 5 to 8), shared as glm_cuda's.
-const gb10_window_costs = costTable(max_rows, 52.0, 6.8);
-const gb10_shared_costs = costTable(engine.shared_rows, 76.0, 4.1);
+/// With DFlash2: a verify forward's ms by rows on two GB10s, fitted on this pair from 587 TF_GLM_DFLASH2_TRACE
+/// records over forced widths 1..8 (lone: 38.73 + 5.68 a row, r2 0.9983; shared forwards by total rows:
+/// 47.38 + 5.05, r2 0.9934). The earlier 52.0/6.8 and 76.0/4.1 over-priced a forward by 34% and 60% at one row,
+/// which starved depth.zig's overhead learner (ms - forward, clamped at zero): of 139 measured two-lane forwards
+/// only 4 could have fired it, against 133 at these prices, where it learns 3 to 8 ms.
+const gb10_window_costs = costTable(max_rows, 38.73, 5.68);
+const gb10_shared_costs = costTable(engine.shared_rows, 47.38, 5.05);
 
 fn costTable(comptime n: usize, comptime one: f64, comptime row: f64) [n]lanes.config.Cost {
     var c: [n]lanes.config.Cost = undefined;
